{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "20499",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 1.28,
      "end_seconds": 6.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting, come in. What do you need help with?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 8.33,
      "end_seconds": 12.69,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "I've been dealing with a mole that has changed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.18,
      "end_seconds": 20.03,
      "duration_seconds": 6.85,
      "text": "Understood. What about a dark patch with an uneven edge, have you noticed that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 21.48,
      "end_seconds": 22.94,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Yeah, that too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.78,
      "end_seconds": 28.57,
      "duration_seconds": 4.79,
      "text": "Did you get lumps in the armpit, weight loss or pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 30.43,
      "end_seconds": 36.3,
      "duration_seconds": 5.87,
      "text": "No lumps in the armpit, weight loss or pain, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.91,
      "end_seconds": 39.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "How about night sweats?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 41.35,
      "end_seconds": 43.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "No, no night sweats."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 44.18,
      "end_seconds": 46.15,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Yes. Neurologically, anything strange?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 47.82,
      "end_seconds": 50.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.19,
      "end_seconds": 54.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.68,
      "text": "Have you ever had an operation?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.17,
      "end_seconds": 60.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "So, I had my womb taken out fifteen years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 71.75,
      "end_seconds": 74.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.74,
      "end_seconds": 83.85,
      "duration_seconds": 7.11,
      "text": "Yes, arthritis in my knees. Yeah, I've had depression for nearly five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 85.2,
      "end_seconds": 94.79,
      "duration_seconds": 9.59,
      "text": "Right, so arthritis in your knees is already on your record. We'll keep that in mind today. Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 96.61,
      "end_seconds": 108.29,
      "duration_seconds": 11.68,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother. I work in accounts at a hospital. I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.2,
      "end_seconds": 114.25,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 115.97,
      "end_seconds": 121.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.98,
      "text": "I'm on something called dicl... diclofenac, 50 milligrams, maybe, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.76,
      "end_seconds": 128.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.57,
      "text": "Do you have the packet or the prescription with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.73,
      "end_seconds": 141.67,
      "duration_seconds": 11.94,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Fluoxetine. I take it 20 milligrams, every morning. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.74,
      "end_seconds": 163.51,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "Do you react to any medicines or foods? Any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 164.36,
      "end_seconds": 170.15,
      "duration_seconds": 5.79,
      "text": "Not currently, but as a youngster tramadol gave me feeling very drowsy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.97,
      "end_seconds": 174.62,
      "duration_seconds": 2.65,
      "text": "Let me quickly check your readings."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.49,
      "end_seconds": 183.74,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Okay, this won't take long..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.05,
      "end_seconds": 210.52,
      "duration_seconds": 10.47,
      "text": "Okay: BP is 120 over 77, respiratory rate 16, temp 36.6 degrees, SpO2 98 percent on room air, pulse is 69 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.6,
      "end_seconds": 214.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.41,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 216.04,
      "end_seconds": 219.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.82,
      "text": "I'll explain what these mean in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.96,
      "end_seconds": 224.52,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Now I'm going to do a short physical check."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 226.36,
      "end_seconds": 227.68,
      "duration_seconds": 1.32,
      "text": "Does that hurt?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.36,
      "end_seconds": 240.73,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "I can't feel any glands in the armpit or neck."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 243.17,
      "end_seconds": 246.33,
      "duration_seconds": 3.16,
      "text": "So, thank you, you can get dressed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 262.12,
      "end_seconds": 281.11,
      "duration_seconds": 18.99,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. I think we're dealing with a pigmented lesion that needs removal for a proper diagnosis at this stage. Let me repeat that back to make sure. You've had a mole that has changed, and no pain or lumps in the armpit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.18,
      "end_seconds": 283.77,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Mm, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.59,
      "end_seconds": 314.13,
      "duration_seconds": 28.54,
      "text": "We should do a skin biopsy for changing mole. We should do a dermoscopy for changing mole. Cover up and use factor 50 sunscreen on exposed skin. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 314.88,
      "end_seconds": 316.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.61,
      "text": "I'll remember that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 318.06,
      "end_seconds": 331.11,
      "duration_seconds": 13.05,
      "text": "The thing that would worry me is if the mole bleeds or grows quickly. If that happens, go to emergency. I'd like you back in two weeks. That's all from me. Any questions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 332.37,
      "end_seconds": 334.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "Thank you, doctor, goodbye."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 336.26,
      "end_seconds": 337.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.28,
      "text": "See you soon."
    }
  ]
}